A||||22||Richard Parnell||How many V8 Fieros?||||5||
Z||000000||Richard Parnell||02-15-2000||07:14 PM||||How many of the forum users out there have V8s in their Fieros?  I know Batboy has one, who else? (he and I have discussed the v8 issue before) I'm just curious 'cause as I've said before I am planning on putting one in my 87.  Only thing (other than money) right now is that my SC has been in a wreck.  You wouldn't know it from looking but upon closer observation I can see the hood is a little off set  (right blinker broken)and there is some bent metal around the ac compressor area.  So I'm trying to determine if this car is worth putting the effort into. It's such a nice looking SC but I want things to be as kosher as possible before expending the time, energy and money.  Anyway, I guess I'm trying to get as many sources for info as possible.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Phil||02-15-2000||07:37 PM||||I might be slightly biased but S/C 3800s are  nice(better than some clunky ole V8). Plus when you blow by Mustangs,Hondas older Vettes etc. you can always say it's just a V6.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Richard Parnell||02-15-2000||08:24 PM||||I can can do the V8 conversion a lot cheaper than the 3800.  Besides I love the way V8s feel and sound.||||reg||11
Z||000003||batboy||02-15-2000||09:08 PM||||Richard, if all the steering and suspension is ok, then I don't see that there would be a problem using your 87 SC. If it's been tweaked enough for the alignment to be out (i.e. tires wearing funny or it pulls to one side) you may want to have a frame shop look at it. Have have it. Is your 2.5 still in good running condition? I'm looking for a 87 4 cylinder engine.||||reg||1
