Z||000008||batboy||02-16-2000||07:22 AM||||Doughboy, a complete V8 kit costs about $2000 I think, not including the engine. I believe the basic rule of thumb with any major engine swap is to figure up what you think it'll cost and about how much time you think it'll take to do the work...and then double it.||||reg||1
Z||000009||deceler8||02-16-2000||09:24 AM||||Got a call today regarding a '87 2m4 I can pick up for $200...has been repainted but isn't running...has a 5 speed...<P>So you're saying about $2,000 for the V8 kit and let's assume $1,000 for a decent V8...hmmm...anyone in the upper Midwest who does that kind of work ?||||reg||10
Z||000010||HarryG||02-16-2000||02:52 PM||||Hey Spyder,<BR>Can you get your decklid closed with that air cleaner mounted?  Every other carbed swap I've seen uses the small triangular shaped cleaners which seem to fit, but I don't think they're too great for air flow capacity.<BR>BTW, I'm in the same situation as Richard Parnell--still looking and dreaming of V8's.<BR>Harry<BR>86GT ||||reg||5
Z||000011||Richard Parnell||02-16-2000||03:21 PM||||Batboy-  The 4 cyl. I have in the car runs real strong still even with over 100K+ miles.  Actually I am really impressed how fast that little 4 banger is.  As far as getting the engine to you, remember I live in Hawaii so shipping might be a little pricey.  Once I do the swap, I'll give you the engine if you will pay shipping.  Re: the alignment, the car steers straight, no pulling, I can let go of the wheel and on a good road it will track straight forever.  I am going to redo the rotors, calipers and as much suspension as is necessary.  I'm undecided if I want to use V8 Archies kit or the one from tech@shelbycustom.com, no exhaust, no extra radiator but it does look like I wouldn't have to move the engine into the wheel well because they have (I think) the shortened driverside axle.  But,the Archie kit looks more complete.  Right now tho it's tax time and I'm getting killed this year, gotta take a loan just to pay those leeches in Washington (sorry, don't get me started)<BR>I had a dream last night in which the conversion was done already.  It was rather disappointing to wake up and realize that it wasn't so.<BR>Spyder- About you car, all I can say is Awesome!<BR>||||reg||7
Z||000012||Monkeyman||02-16-2000||06:22 PM||||deceler8--Archie (of V8Archie and Technet fame) is located in Chicago.  He's a male appendage, but he's supposed to be the best at V8 swaps.||||reg||1
Z||000013||Spyder||02-16-2000||11:25 PM||||Let’s see, this is off the top of my head, so sorry if I forget something.<BR>The engine is a New GM Goodwrench 350 crate motor bored out to be a 355.  <BR>Installed a mid-range cam.<BR>It’s the older style V8 with the two part rear seal.  <BR>MSD 6AL ignition blaster 2 coil<BR>MSD distributor with a Moroso correct a cap. Notice plug wires don’t cross.<BR>Weiand intake,<BR>Holley 4 barl Carb Mechanical Secondaries Double Pumper Polished electric choke, (can’t remember the number right off)<BR>Holley external fuel pump and regulator<BR>Stock Chevy exhaust manifolds.<BR>I used V8 Archie’s  master build kit. (lots of cool performance stuff)<BR>And I’m sure I forgot something.<BR>If I knew then, what I know now, I would have done things a little different.  I took advice from someone who I thought knew how to build engines. But I am extremely happy with the power and ohhhh the sound.  The torque is wonderful.  You can start in any gear. Kick it in any gear, your neck snaps back.<P>I did swap the 4 speed for a 5 speed. I wanted the extra gear.<P>Batboy I would be honored if you want to use the pics.<P>HarryG That is a temporary air cleaner until I come up with something custom.  The triangle one is supposed to be one of the best low profiles, the whole thing has holes all over it for air.<P>V8 Archie was good to work with. He helped out with my questions and he sent an installation video. He was a little slow shipping but that didn’t slow me down. (me, snails pace)<P>Thanks everyone, I’m very proud, lots of time and money, Thanks.<BR>||||reg||7
Z||000014||Phaeton||02-16-2000||11:45 PM||||Those stock chevy manifolds look like '65 corvette ramshead with two and one half inch outlets, right up there with block hugger headers for performance.||||reg||1
Z||000015||batboy||02-17-2000||07:28 AM||||I"ve used those ram's horn exhaust manifolds on a couple streetrods before, they work nice especially if you have a tight fit.||||reg||1
Z||000016||pherder||02-18-2000||07:38 PM||||When Archie posted on the Technet that he was offering 10% off anything on his site (just before Chrismas ... it is over now  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> )<BR>I emailed him and made a purchase of his basic install kit and a 4 core radiator.  <P>Mind you, this was one week BEFORE Christmas!!!<P>I had the parts on the 23rd!!!  It was the Fastest service I have EVER gotten!!!<P>Paul<BR>||||reg||14
Z||000017||Richard Parnell||02-18-2000||08:41 PM||||Pherder-  What are you doing to your car?  Do you think the basic kit will be enough.  I do know that it's tough to build an exhaust for this install. A guy I know built his own and it leaks like crazy.  I think you have to start with at least the corvette exhaust manifold for space considerations.||||reg||5
Z||000018||batboy||02-18-2000||09:11 PM||||Paul is a maniac custom Fiero builder. Don't worry about him, he's an advanced engine swapper guy. He has some nice toys.||||reg||1
Z||000019||pherder||02-18-2000||09:40 PM||||Richard,<P>As Batboy put it so nicely, I am going bonzo in Fiero swaps ... Quad 4 in my 88 Coupe, 3.1 into my 88 GT and the TPI into the 88 Formula.  <P>I will be using Sanderson's CC90 VERY short headers  <A HREF="http://www.centuryperformance.com/sanderson20.htm#CC90" TARGET=_blank>http://www.centuryperformance.com/sanderson20.htm#CC90</A>  and a custom built, dual exhaust system ... maybe.  I will lose the bottom of the trunk if I do a dual exhaust but will not if I do a two into one.  I have one of FOCOA's "new" replacement mufflers and may use it with dual tiny cat. converters.<P>I purchased V8Archie's master kit a couple of years ago (for my first but aborted V8 swap) and this time felt like I could get the stuff I wanted instead of using some of his and basically pitching the rest.  I wanted "prettier" stuff where Archie's stuff would have worked, just wasn't "showie".<P>Paul||||reg||10
Z||000020||batboy||02-19-2000||09:51 AM||||Ok, so how many of the Forum members actually have V8 Fieros (yes a half finished project does count, when are they ever completely done?) I know Richard and several others have been thinking about it. I sure got a lot of emails last summer from people who were interested in doing the swap.<P>1) Eric's white 88 GT <BR>2) Paul's TBI 88 Formula<BR>3) My silver 85 Batmobile<BR>4) Spyder's Fiero (see pics above)<BR>5) Dan-o's kit car<BR>6) FieroV8's 85 SE (see below)<P>Anyone else?<p>[This message has been edited by batboy (edited 02-21-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000021||fierov8||02-21-2000||03:11 PM||||....decloaking..........<P>I'm currently in process with a V8 swap.  The details are:<P>Car:  '86 SE, '88 cradle/susp., GT rear clip<P>Interior:  Custom, started with a PISA ZR2 kit and added custom aluminum dash insert, VDO gauges, rollbar, Jamex seats.<P>Engine (the part of the course you've been waiting for):  <BR>1991 SBC 350, L98, aluminum heads (Corvette).<BR>TPIS ZZ9 Cam<BR>TPIS mini ram intake<BR>Bored .030<BR>Barrier coatings on the pistons<BR>Balanced and blueprinted<BR>2.02/1.56 valves<BR>multi-angle valve job<BR>full porting from intake through head<P>......and who knows what else!!  Engine is still in process.  Once done, it will be dropped into the car.  Engine swap kit is a one-off from one of the guys behind the Northstar kit offered by DesignOne.  Uses an aluminum adapter plate and Mark Williams Chrome Moly axles (yes, the engine is shifted 2.5" to the left and the drvr side frame rail will be "adapted" to fit.<P>Hoping to be drivable for part of the SCCA season here in Emod.<P>Pics and a web page hoping to happen some day.............<P>-jeffd<P>||||reg||12
Z||000022||bwayne||02-22-2000||11:19 PM||||I've got an 85 coupe with a 355:<BR>Erson cams/lifters<BR>Roller tip rockers<BR>Pete Jackson noisy gear drive<BR>Sanderson block hugger headers<BR>Edelbrock manifold<BR>Holley 600 w/vacuum secondary<BR>Weiand air cleaner<BR>Just finishing custom dual exhaust-no cats<P>Sort of anxious to see if the exhaust makes a difference.<P>As the body is not the best, I'm thinking of<BR>a kit car for this one.||||reg||10
